1040:	\subsection{Design-theoretic approach}\label{subsection 5.2}
1041:	In this subsection, we use nonvanishing flats to show that vanishing flats of extendable bent functions must be highly structured combinatorial objects, from what follows, that the existence of certain subdesigns in $\VF(F)$ is a measure of extendability of an $(n,m)$-bent function $F$.
